<title>USA: United Video chairman/CEO resigns.</title>
<headline>United Video chairman/CEO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>TULSA, Okla. 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Video Satellite Group Inc said Wednesday that Lawrence Flinn Jr had resigned as chairman and chief executive officer, effective January 1.</p>
<p>It said Larry Romrell would become the non-executive chairman of United Video.  </p>
<p>Romrell is currently president and CEO of TCI Technology Ventures Inc, a subsidiary of Tele-Communications Inc, United Video said.</p>
<p>Flinn is retiring for health reasons but will continue as non-executive vice chairman of the board, the company said.</p>
<p>Roy Bliss will continue as president and chief operating officer, it added.</p>
<p>The company said it was not naming a new CEO, nor was it searching for one at this time.</p>
</text>
